 is all kinds of meta commentary of  marvel breaking the fourth wall and just  poking a bit of fun of themselves but  after this the impossible man actually  stays around for quite a few issues and  helps out the team while reed and ben  are trapped in the negatives up as for  his powers his primary ability is that  he can rearrange the molecules that  basically make up his anatomy to take on  any form he chooses not only can he copy  the shape of anything or anyone but like  i said earlier he can also mimic the  abilities of super powered individuals  like he did with cyclops and his optic  blasts and he also mimicked the powers  of all four members of the fantastic  four magneto and wasp among others but  his molecular manipulation abilities are  not limited to simply changing his size  and his shape he also is able to change  the composition of his body to differing  materials such as changing into a sheet  of solid steel or becoming one of the  galaxy's heaviest materials so that ben  grimm cannot lift him he can also change  his state of matter to liquid or gas if  he chooses and when he decided to become  water he was able to extinguish the  human torch's flank now he also has  repeatedly demonstrated inability to  duplicate himself and even created a  wife and several thousand children for  himself which all share the same  consciousness and has claimed that he  has the capacity to create nine billion  unique beings now although impossible  man is not known for his fighting  ability he has been able to hold his own  with some pretty heavy hitters the  reason for this is not really due to his  offensive capabilities even though he  had knocked the thing through a wall  after he transformed his fists and  mjolnir but because of his insane  durability he's been punched by the hulk  without being injured and even recovered  from an attack from the molecule man  who's one of the most powerful  characters in the marvel universe and  after he recovers he develops an  immunity to the molecule man's molecular  manipulation abilities and arguably his  most impressive feat he was able to  resist the reality warping powers of  amatsu mikabashi the chaos king and if  you're not familiar with who that guy is  he's one of the biggest threats that the  marvel universe has ever seen and  actually threatened the existence of the  marvel multiverse and even though  impossible man was eventually  overpowered by the chaos king the fact  that he was able to mount any resistance  at all when some of the most powerful  heroes were completely unable to do so  is a testament to just how powerful the  impossible man is and also suggests that  he himself possesses reality warping  abilities in addition to matter  manipulation now this is further  supported by the fact that he's been  able to control time and create powers  which beasts of the x-men described as  reality bending technology on another  occasion impossible man was able to  combine the hulk and red hulk into a  singular entity called the compound hulk  that was literally half red and half  green and ridiculous looking as it  sounds right it looked ridiculous but it  was cool and even galactus has attested  to impossible man's insane power level  stating that in his own way impossible  man represented as big of a threat as  the phoenix force now if you're a fan of  dc comics you may have noticed a lot of  similarity between the impossible man  and mr millennial a frequent antagonist  of superman who also possesses reality  warping abilities and in fact these two  characters actually cross paths back  when marvel and dc we're willing to work  together instead of acting like petulant  children and creating stories for both  sides to enjoy and bicker over endlessly  as to whether or not it was the right  choice  but regardless these two actually battle  pretty evenly for most of the issue and  although we don't see who wins the fact  that impossible man could seemingly  stalemate mr moon 